<td tEditID="c1r1" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; color:#000000; bEditID:r3st1; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r1" locked="0" >
<![CDATA[<font face="arial">{!Contact.FirstName},</font><div><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div><font face="arial"><div>Thank you for your interest in the College of Nursing and Health Innovation at Arizona State University.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Our postbaccalaureate (PBAC) Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) program allows students with a bachelor's degree in a non-nursing field from a regionally accredited institution to complete their BSN through one year of full-time study at ASU’s Downtown Phoenix campus. Graduates of the PBAC program are eligible to sit for the licensing exam to become a Registered Nurse (RN).&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Students are admitted annually in the spring, and the deadline to apply each year is <b>September 1</b>. Placement in the program is based on clinical space availability.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>To learn more about this exciting option, including admission requirements and the placement process, attend a <a href="https://nursingandhealth.asu.edu/admissions/information-sessions">BSN Information Session</a> either in-person or online. Once you have attended a BSN Information Session, you will be provided with instructions to apply for admission and learn about how your credits transfer to ASU.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>We hope this information helps answer your questions. If you need additional assistance, please don’t hesitate to contact us.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Sincerely,</div><div><br></div><div>Recruitment and Admissions</div><div>College of Nursing and Health Innovation</div><div>Phone: 602-496-0937</div><div>Office Hours: Monday - Friday, 8 a.m. - 5 p.m.</div><div><a href="mailto:conhi_undergrad@asu.edu">conhi_undergrad@asu.edu</a></div><div><a href="https://nursingandhealth.asu.edu/">nursingandhealth.asu.edu</a></div></font></div>]]></td>
</tr>
</table>